/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  liquidDensity02_waterEthanol -- D2 of the liquid-density pilot (C378).
  Water + ethanol, x_ethanol 0.25 (w_ethanol 0.4602), 298.15 K, 1 bar.  The
  kernel prices {ethanol, water} by idealMixing: water by its IAPWS-95
  reference equation, ethanol by its record's 25 C volume carried by
  Rackett.  ADDITIVE VOLUMES HAVE NO EXCESS VOLUME: the measured mixture is
  denser (Pecar and Dolecek 2005, 0.1 MPa: the method is 1.76 % low on
  average at 298.15 K, 2.06 % at 323.15 K; about -1 cm3/mol of excess volume
  at x = 0.4 that no leaf can supply).  The pilot SCORES 298.15 and
  323.15 K and REPORTS 348.15 K, where the ethanol leaf (-1.9 %) is the
  error (thresholds note 3.2 and DEV.md 4c C378).

  The flowsheet of every liquid-density demonstration: feed (1 kg/s) ->
  pump P1 (dP 2 bar, eta 0.7) -> CSTR R1 (V_R 1 m3, the reaction's reactant
  absent, see constant/reactions) -> product.  By hand, with rho the
  property kernel's liquid density printed in the run's table:
      Q   = m_dot / rho                 (the pump's volumetric flow)
      W   = Q dP / eta                  (its shaft power)
      h   = dP / (rho g)                (its head)
      tau = V_R rho / m_dot             (the CSTR's residence time, at its
                                         feed, the pump's outlet state)
  The pump prices its INLET state, the CSTR its FEED (the pump's outlet).
  THE PUMP'S FIRST LAW IS OPEN, AND PINNED (check_energy_closure, 70 %):
  the residual is exactly the useful shaft work, eta x W_shaft, which the
  generic liquid enthalpy (no pressure term) cannot hold -- the pump's own
  advisory says so -- and commission C390 closes it.
  Theory Guide: sec:liquid-density-methods.  Gate: check_density_pilot.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        P1;
        type        pump;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( pumped );
        operation   { dP 2 bar; eta 0.7; }
    }
    {
        name        R1;
        type        cstr;
        in          pumped;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation   { V_R 1; }
        reactions   ( absentAcid );
    }
);
